I chose all four state‑feedback weights to be negative so that the force always pushes opposite to the sign of the state (position, angle, cart velocity, and angular velocity), yielding a classic proportional‑derivative controller for the cart‑pole. The magnitudes are modest (≈0.5–2.0) to keep the combined action well within the ±3 N limit for typical safe state ranges (|x|≤0.2 m, |θ|≤0.2 rad, |ẋ|≈1 m/s, |θ̇|≈2 rad/s), thus avoiding saturation and chattering seen in many low‑reward policies. A zero bias removes any constant drift, letting the linear feedback alone recentre the cart and stabilize the pole from small perturbations. This balanced, low‑gain controller should explore the corrective region of the policy space and has a good chance of achieving a substantially higher return than the previously sampled drift‑biased configurations.
