response-og: params[0] = -0.5, params[1] = 6.0, params[2] = -0.3, params[3] = 2.5, params[4] = 0.0  
Explanation: Positive w1 in previous high‑score policies (≈0.5) consistently caused cart‑position feedback that pushed the cart further away from the center, leading to systematic drift and early termination at the position limits. By switching w1 to a modest negative value (‑0.5) we introduce restoring force proportional to cart displacement, pulling the cart back toward the origin when it drifts right and pushing it right when it drifts left. The angle gain w2 remains high (≈6) to provide strong corrective force in the direction of pole tilt, while w3 stays negative (‑0.3) to damp cart velocity and w4 stays around 2.5 to react to angular velocity. Keeping the bias at zero avoids adding constant offset, allowing the controller to rely on state feedback. This combination should preserve the effective pole‑angle and angular‑velocity regulation seen in the ~250‑step policies while correcting the cart‑position drift, potentially pushing performance well beyond the current best.
